From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Subject: [PATCH] net: bcmgenet: mask the discard counter out of the RX
 producer index

RDMA_PROD_INDEX holds the producer index in bits 15:0 and, in bits
31:16, the number of frames the controller discarded because no receive
descriptor was free (Linux: DMA_P_INDEX_MASK, DMA_P_INDEX_DISCARD_CNT).
The driver compared the whole register with its 16-bit consumer index.
Once a frame has been discarded the two never match again: recv() then
hands out descriptors the controller has not filled, with stale lengths
and old frame data, and TCP and TFTP transfers stall until they time out.

rx_ring_init() took the whole register as the start index too, so a
discard count left by an earlier user of the controller (the previous
network command, or the OS before a warm reboot) had the same effect
after the first frame.

Mask the index in both places, as Linux does.

Seen on the Raspberry Pi 400: wget fails with "HTTP client error 5" and
TFTP with "Timeout!" on large files, often right after a reboot, while
the MAC's MIB counters show no FCS, alignment, length or overrun errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/bcmgenet.c b/drivers/net/bcmgenet.c
index a0264dc3..fec0afdd 100644
--- a/drivers/net/bcmgenet.c
+++ b/drivers/net/bcmgenet.c
@@ -136,6 +136,9 @@
 #define DMA_DESC_ADDRESS_LO		0x04
 #define DMA_DESC_ADDRESS_HI		0x08
 #define DMA_DESC_SIZE			12
+/* RDMA_PROD_INDEX: the producer index in bits 15:0, the count of frames
+ * discarded for lack of a free descriptor in bits 31:16 */
+#define DMA_P_INDEX_MASK		0xffff
 
 #define GENET_RX_OFF			0x2000
 #define GENET_RDMA_REG_OFF					\
@@ -335,7 +338,8 @@ static int bcmgenet_gmac_eth_recv(struct udevice *dev,
 {
 	struct bcmgenet_eth_priv *priv = dev_get_priv(dev);
 	void *desc_base = priv->rx_desc_base + priv->rx_index * DMA_DESC_SIZE;
-	u32 prod_index = readl(priv->mac_reg + RDMA_PROD_INDEX);
+	u32 prod_index = readl(priv->mac_reg + RDMA_PROD_INDEX) &
+			 DMA_P_INDEX_MASK;
 	u32 length, addr;
 
 	if (prod_index == priv->c_index)
@@ -406,7 +410,8 @@ static void rx_ring_init(struct bcmgenet_eth_priv *priv)
 	       priv->mac_reg + RDMA_RING_REG_BASE + DMA_END_ADDR);
 
 	/* cannot init RDMA_PROD_INDEX to 0, so align RDMA_CONS_INDEX on it instead */
-	priv->c_index = readl(priv->mac_reg + RDMA_PROD_INDEX);
+	priv->c_index = readl(priv->mac_reg + RDMA_PROD_INDEX) &
+			DMA_P_INDEX_MASK;
 	writel(priv->c_index, priv->mac_reg + RDMA_CONS_INDEX);
 	priv->rx_index = priv->c_index;
 	priv->rx_index &= 0xFF;
-- 
